# Privilege Escalation

After sending the malicious request, the account page was refreshed.

An **Admin Panel** link became available to the authenticated `wiener` user.

This confirmed that the polluted `isAdmin` property was being used by the application's authorization logic.

The resulting attack chain was:

```text
POST /my-account/change-address
             |
             v
        __proto__
             |
             v
Object.prototype.isAdmin = true
             |
             v
      user.isAdmin
             |
             v
    Authorization check
             |
             v
       Admin Panel
             |
             v
    Privilege Escalation
```

The administrator panel was accessed and the `carlos` user was deleted.

The lab was then successfully solved.

