# Conclusions

The application was vulnerable to **Server-Side Prototype Pollution** through the `__proto__` property accepted by the `/my-account/change-address` endpoint.

The vulnerability was initially confirmed by injecting an arbitrary `foo` property and observing that it appeared in the returned user object without being explicitly defined.

Further investigation identified `isAdmin` as a security-sensitive gadget. By injecting:

```json
"__proto__": {
    "isAdmin": true
}
```

the attacker was able to influence the value resolved by the application's authorization logic.

This resulted in unauthorized access to the administrator panel and allowed the attacker to delete the `carlos` user.

The vulnerability therefore demonstrates the complete exploitation chain:

```text
Attacker-Controlled JSON
        ↓
    __proto__
        ↓
Prototype Pollution
        ↓
   isAdmin = true
        ↓
Authorization Bypass
        ↓
Privilege Escalation
        ↓
Administrative Access
```

The lab was successfully exploited and solved.
